.SH "NAME"
miktex-bibtex \- make a bibliography for LaTeX
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBmiktex\-bibtex\fR\ 'u
\fBmiktex\-bibtex\fR [\fIoption\fR...] \fIauxfile\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This man page is an adaption of the corresponding
TeX Live
man page\&.
.PP
BibTeX
reads the top\-level auxiliary (\&.aux) file that was output during the running of
\fBmiktex-latex\fR(1)\fBmiktex-tex\fR(1)
and creates a bibliography (\&.bbl) file that will be
.\" .bbl (bibliography file)
incorporated into the document on subsequent runs of
LaTeX
or
TeX\&.
.\" bibliography: creation
.PP
BibTeX
looks up, in bibliographic database
.\" .bib (bibliographic database)
(\&.bib) files specified by the
\fB\ebibliography\fR
command, the entries specified by the
\fB\ecite\fR
and
\fB\enocite\fR
commands in the
LaTeX
or
TeX
source file\&. It formats the information from those entries according to instructions in a bibliography style (\&.bst) file
.\" .bst (bibliography style file)
(specified by the
\fB\ebibliographystyle\fR
command, and it outputs the results to the
\&.bbl.\" .bbl
file\&.
.PP
The
LaTeX
reference manual explains what a
LaTeX
source file must contain to work with
BibTeX\&. Appendix\ \&B of the manual describes the format of the
\&.bib
files\&. The
BibTeXing
document describes extensions and details of this format, and it gives other useful hints for using
BibTeX\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-alias=\fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
Pretend to be program
\fIname\fR, i\&.e\&., set program (and memory dump) name to
\fIname\fR\&.
.\" --alias=name
This may affect the search paths and other values used\&. Using this option is equivalent to copying the program file to
\fIname\fR
and invoking
\fIname\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-disable\-installer\fR
.RS 4
Disable automatic installation of packages\&.
.\" --disable-installer
Specifying this option overrules settings in the
MiKTeX
configuration data store\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-enable\-installer\fR
.RS 4
Enable automatic installation of packages\&.
.\" --enable-installer
Specifying this option overrules settings in the
MiKTeX
configuration data store\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
.\" --help
Give help and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-hhelp\fR
.RS 4
.\" --hhelp
This option is only available on
Windows
systems: show the manual page in an HTML Help window and exit when the window is closed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-include\-directory=\fR\fB\fIdir\fR\fR
.RS 4
Add the directory
\fIdir\fR
to the
.\" --include-directory=dir
head of the list of directories to be searched for input files\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-min\-crossrefs=\fR\fB\fIn\fR\fR
.RS 4
.\" --min-crossrefs=n
Defines the minimum number of
\fBcrossref\fRs required for automatic inclusion of the
.\" cross-references: minimum number required
crossref\*(Aqd entry on the citation list; the default is two\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
.RS 4
.\" --quiet
Suppress all output, except errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-record\-package\-usages=\fR\fB\fIfile\fR\fR
.RS 4
Record all package usages and write
.\" --record-package-usages=file
them into
\fIfile\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-trace\fR\fB[=\fItracestreams\fR]\fR
.RS 4
Enable trace messages\&.
.\" --trace=tracestreams
The
\fItracestreams\fR
argument, if specified, is a comma\-separated list of trace stream names (Chapter\ \&9, Trace Streams)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
.\" --version
Show version information and exit\&.
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.PP
\fBBIBINPUTS\fR
.RS 4
.\" BIBINPUTS
Extra paths to locate
\&.bib
files\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBBSTINPUTS\fR
.RS 4
.\" BSTINPUTS
Extra paths to locate
\&.bst
files\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBMIKTEX_TRACE\fR
.RS 4
.\" MIKTEX_TRACE
Comma\-separated list of trace stream names (see
Chapter\ \&9, Trace Streams)\&. If this variable is set, then
MiKTeX
programs will write trace messages into the configured log sink\&.
.RE
